# Check out with LF everywhere, including on Windows.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout converts every text file to CRLF and
# `wrangler deploy` uploads those bytes, so what is served stops matching what
# is in the repo — one extra byte per line across the whole app. It is benign
# for HTML and CSS, but it breaks two things that are supposed to be checkable:
# the prompt hash in `model-participant.mjs --check`, which compares the repo's
# prompt against the artefact it produced, and any attempt to verify that what
# the audience is being served is what was reviewed.
#
# There is no build step here — files go to Cloudflare exactly as checked out —
# so the checkout is the deployment, and it needs to be byte-stable.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary. Must never be line-ending converted or they are corrupt on arrival.
*.woff2 binary
*.woff   binary
*.ttf    binary
*.otf    binary
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.ico    binary
*.pdf    binary
*.pptx   binary
